{"units": [{"id": "anaptysso-quote2", "translation": "having unfolded all the suffering."}, {"id": "anarithmos-orth1", "translation": "countless"}, {"id": "anarithmos-def1", "translation": "countless"}, {"id": "anarithmos-quote1", "translation": "terrible and countless in number."}, {"id": "anarkton_see-orth1", "translation": "unruled"}, {"id": "anarkton_see-note1", "translation": "[corrupt for ἀνάρχετον [unruled], which see.]"}, {"id": "anarkton_see-word1", "translation": "unruled"}, {"id": "anarpazo-orth1", "translation": "to snatch away"}, {"id": "anarpazo-def1", "translation": "to snatch away"}, {"id": "anarpazo-quote1", "translation": "beware the rushing blast, lest it snatch you away."}, {"id": "anarpaxandran_see-orth1", "translation": "man-snatching"}, {"id": "anarpaxandran_see-note1", "translation": "[corrupt for τὰν ἁρπαξάνδραν [the man-snatching one]. See ἁρπάξανδρος [man-snatching].]"}, {"id": "anarpaxandran_see-word1", "translation": "the man-snatching one"}, {"id": "anarpaxandran_see-word2", "translation": "man-snatching"}, {"id": "anarroibdeo-orth1", "translation": "to gulp down again"}, {"id": "anarroibdeo-def1", "translation": "to gulp down again"}, {"id": "anarroibdeo-note1", "translation": "αναρροιβδεῖ [gulps down again] is explained by ἀναρροφεῖ [sucks up again], but he adds that Aeschylus (fr. 217) said it for διαπνεῖ [breathes through], which Meineke changes to ἀναπνεῖ [breathes up] in Philologus vol. 13 p. 515."}, {"id": "anarroibdeo-quote1", "translation": "gulps down again"}, {"id": "anarroibdeo-quote2", "translation": "sucks up again"}, {"id": "anarroibdeo-word1", "translation": "breathes through"}, {"id": "anarroibdeo-word2", "translation": "breathes up"}, {"id": "anarsios-orth1", "translation": "hostile"}, {"id": "anarsios-def1", "translation": "hostile"}, {"id": "anarsios-quote1", "translation": "you were hostile enough by the Scamander."}, {"id": "anarchetos-orth1", "translation": "without a ruler"}, {"id": "anarchetos-def1", "translation": "without a ruler"}, {"id": "anarchetos-note1", "translation": "Similarly ἀπευκτός [not prayed for] and ἀπεύχετος [not prayed for] are said."}, {"id": "anarchetos-quote1", "translation": "neither praise a life without a ruler (thus Wieseler for ἄναρκτον [unruled]) nor one ruled by a master."}, {"id": "anarchetos-word1", "translation": "not prayed for"}, {"id": "anarchetos-word2", "translation": "not prayed for"}, {"id": "anarchia-orth1", "translation": "anarchy"}, {"id": "anarchia-def1", "translation": "absence of rule, lack of rulers"}, {"id": "anarchia-def2", "translation": "refusal of obedience"}, {"id": "anarchia-quote1", "translation": "will you not speak of anarchy?"}, {"id": "anarchia-quote2", "translation": "holding this untrustworthy anarchy for the city."}, {"id": "anarchia-quote3", "translation": "anarchy voiced by the people."}, {"id": "anarchos-orth1", "translation": "without a leader"}, {"id": "anarchos-def1", "translation": "without a leader"}, {"id": "anarchos-note1", "translation": "in verses composed by an interpolator in imitation of the words of v. 526.]"}, {"id": "anarchos-quote1", "translation": "neither unruled nor ruled by a master,"}, {"id": "anaspao-orth1", "translation": "to drink in"}, {"id": "anaspao-def1", "translation": "to drink in"}, {"id": "anaspao-quote1", "translation": "but when the dust drinks up a man's blood."}, {"id": "anassa-orth1", "translation": "queen"}, {"id": "anassa-def1", "translation": "queen, title of goddesses"}, {"id": "anassa-def2", "translation": "queen (of mortals)"}, {"id": "anassa-quote1", "translation": "blessed queen Onca."}, {"id": "anassa-quote2", "translation": "queen Athena."}, {"id": "anassa-quote3", "translation": "queen of this land, Athena."}, {"id": "anassa-quote4", "translation": "O queen of the deep-girdled Persian women."}, {"id": "anassa-quote5", "translation": "queen of this land."}, {"id": "anasso-orth1", "translation": "to rule"}, {"id": "anasso-def1", "translation": "to rule"}, {"id": "anasso-quote1", "translation": "so that Zeus might rule, forsooth."}, {"id": "anasso-quote2", "translation": "a phantom will seem to rule the house."}, {"id": "anasso-quote3", "translation": "and Hades may rule over those who died before."}, {"id": "anasso_2-orth1", "translation": "to leap up"}, {"id": "anasso_2-def1", "translation": "to leap up"}, {"id": "anasso_2-note1", "translation": "Which Thomas Magister explains by κρατῶν [ruling]. Correctly Turnebus ἀναίσσων [leaping up], except that he should have written ἀνάσσων [leaping up]."}, {"id": "anasso_2-quote1", "translation": "for the young marrow leaping up within the breast."}, {"id": "anasso_2-quote2", "translation": "who is it that leaps with swift foot of nimble leap?"}, {"id": "anasso_2-word1", "translation": "ruling"}, {"id": "anasso_2-word2", "translation": "leaping up"}, {"id": "anasso_2-word3", "translation": "leaping up"}, {"id": "anastasis-orth1", "translation": "resurrection"}, {"id": "anastasis-def1", "translation": "resurrection, restoration"}, {"id": "anastasis-def2", "translation": "destruction"}, {"id": "anastasis-quote1", "translation": "once a man is dead, there is no resurrection."}, {"id": "anastasis-quote2", "translation": "destructions of cities."}, {"id": "anastasis-quote3", "translation": "the capture and destruction of Troy."}, {"id": "anastater-orth1", "translation": "destroyer"}, {"id": "anastater-def1", "translation": "destroyer"}, {"id": "anastater-quote1", "translation": "destroyer of the land of the Cadmeans."}, {"id": "anastater-quote2", "translation": "destroyers of Troy."}, {"id": "anastates-orth1", "translation": "destroyer"}, {"id": "anastates-def1", "translation": "destroyer"}, {"id": "anastates-quote1", "translation": "destroyer of Ilium."}, {"id": "anastenazo-orth1", "translation": "to groan aloud"}, {"id": "anastenazo-def1", "translation": "to groan aloud"}, {"id": "anastenazo-quote1", "translation": "the twofold tomb-lament groans for you."}, {"id": "anasteno-orth1", "translation": "to groan aloud"}, {"id": "anasteno-def1", "translation": "to groan aloud"}, {"id": "anasteno-note1", "translation": "[On 408 see στένω [to groan].]"}, {"id": "anasteno-quote1", "translation": "how many things from my dim mind make me groan."}, {"id": "anasteno-quote2", "translation": "why then do I, pitiable, groan thus?"}, {"id": "anasteno-word1", "translation": "to groan"}, {"id": "anastrepho-orth1", "translation": "to turn back"}, {"id": "anastrepho-def1", "translation": "to turn back, to turn in the opposite direction"}, {"id": "anastrepho-quote1", "translation": "but tell me this, turning back again."}, {"id": "anastrepho-quote2", "translation": "and a deep stain from the depths turns me back."}, {"id": "anastrophe-orth1", "translation": "turning back"}, {"id": "anastrophe-def1", "translation": "turning back"}, {"id": "anastrophe-quote1", "translation": "the Corycian rock, hollow, bird-loving, turning-place of the gods."}, {"id": "anaschetos-orth1", "translation": "tolerable"}, {"id": "anaschetos-def1", "translation": "tolerable"}, {"id": "anaschetos-quote1", "translation": "falls not to be endured."}, {"id": "anaschetos-quote2", "translation": "creatures not to be endured."}, {"id": "anaschetos-quote3", "translation": "for the wicked, when they prosper, are not to be endured."}, {"id": "anatello-orth1", "translation": "to make rise"}, {"id": "anatello-def1", "translation": "to make rise"}, {"id": "anatello-def2", "translation": "to rise"}, {"id": "anatello-quote1", "translation": "Egypt makes the corn of Demeter rise."}, {"id": "anatello-quote2", "translation": "thick hair rising."}, {"id": "anati-orth1", "translation": "without harm"}, {"id": "anati-def1", "translation": "without harm"}, {"id": "anati-note1", "translation": "Thus I wrote for ανατεί [without harm]: on which see Lexicon Sophocles p. 37."}, {"id": "anati-quote1", "translation": "nourishing without harm"}, {"id": "anati-word1", "translation": "without harm"}, {"id": "anatlao-orth1", "translation": "to endure"}, {"id": "anatlao-def1", "translation": "see ἀνάτλημι [to endure] (although the ancients used neither form, but only the aorist ἔτλην [I endured] of both the simple and compound verbs) to endure, to sustain."}]}